---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Fitness Tracking · Alexander Kashyap"
  description="Fitness Tracking (private project)."
  noindex
  current="private"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/private/fitness.css">
    <script is:inline type="module" src="/private/fitness.js"></script>
  </Fragment>
  <section class="section fit-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="sr-only">Fitness Tracking</h1>
      <!-- Everything below is drawn by private/fitness.js from /private/api/fitness/data
           (worker/fitness.js), which reads the fitness-data repo. No workout data
           is in this file or this repo. -->
      <p class="fit-status" id="fit-status" role="status">Loading your workouts…</p>

      <div id="fit-app" hidden>
        <h2 class="section-title">Up next</h2>
        <div id="fit-next" class="card fit-next"></div>

        <dl class="stat-grid fit-stats" id="fit-stats"></dl>

        <h2 class="section-title fit-h">Body weight</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">From the weigh-ins you give your daily session. They swing a few pounds with water and food, so the line is the 7-day average.</p>
        <div id="fit-weight-chart" class="fit-chart"></div>

        <h2 class="section-title fit-h">Weak areas</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Muscles under the weekly set target, lifts that stopped improving, and push vs pull balance, over the last 4 weeks. The fifth lift of each session goes to the biggest gap.</p>
        <div id="fit-weak" class="grid two"></div>

        <h2 class="section-title fit-h">Strength</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Estimated 1-rep max per session (best set, Epley formula). Bigger dots are new bests.</p>
        <label class="fit-label" for="fit-lift">Lift</label>
        <select id="fit-lift" class="fit-input"></select>
        <div id="fit-strength" class="fit-chart"></div>

        <h2 class="section-title fit-h">Consistency</h2>
        <div id="fit-calendar" class="fit-chart"></div>

        <h2 class="section-title fit-h">Weekly sets per muscle</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Average over the last 4 weeks. Main muscles count a full set, helpers half. The shaded band is the 10 to 20 set target.</p>
        <div id="fit-volume"></div>

        <h2 class="section-title fit-h">Cardio</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Minutes per week by machine. The tick on each week is 25 minutes for every workout you finished.</p>
        <div id="fit-cardio" class="fit-chart"></div>

        <h2 class="section-title fit-h">Previous workouts</h2>
        <div id="fit-history"></div>

        <h2 class="section-title fit-h" id="my-lifts">My lifts</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Rank the lifts you like in each slot; your #1 is suggested first, and what you actually log counts too. "Never" keeps a lift out of your plans. Saving updates the fitness-data repo, and the next plan uses it.</p>
        <div class="toggle" id="fit-days" role="group" aria-label="Day"></div>
        <div id="fit-slots" class="grid two"></div>
        <div class="fit-save">
          <button class="btn primary" type="button" id="fit-save" disabled>Save rankings</button>
          <span class="muted" id="fit-save-status" role="status"></span>
        </div>

        <h3 class="fit-h3">Add a lift</h3>
        <p class="fit-why">Type a lift you want in your plans, in your own words. Your next daily session works out where it fits, adds it, and tells you.</p>
        <form id="fit-request" class="fit-request">
          <input class="fit-input" name="text" maxlength="200" required autocomplete="off" placeholder="e.g. landmine press, love it for shoulders" aria-label="Lift to add">
          <button class="btn primary" type="submit">Add</button>
        </form>
        <p class="muted fit-request-status" id="fit-request-status" role="status"></p>
        <ul class="fit-requests" id="fit-requests" aria-label="Waiting for your next session"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="fit-tip" id="fit-tip" role="tooltip" hidden></div>
</BaseLayout>
